{"name":"Knockout","hex":"#c42b2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"knockout","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of making one unconscious, or at least unable to come back on one's feet within a certain period of time; a TKO.","The deactivation of anything."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Rendering someone unconscious.","Amazing; gorgeous; beautiful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/knockout"}],"entries":[{"title":"Knockout","blocks":[{"text":"A knockout is a fight-ending, winning criterion in several full-contact combat sports, such as boxing, kickboxing, Muay Thai, mixed martial arts, karate, some forms of taekwondo and other sports involving striking, as well as fighting-based video games. A full knockout is considered any legal strike or combination thereof that renders an opponent unable to continue fighting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Ingemar_Johansson_and_Floyd_Pattersson_1959.JPG/330px-Ingemar_Johansson_and_Floyd_Pattersson_1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knockout","wikidata":"Q668642"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg/500px-Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg/1280px-Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg/500px-Muhammad_Ali_fights_Brian_London_on_August_6%2C_1966.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A heavy blo